WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.150
- [Narrator] TikTok is at a crossroads.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.040
Concerns about its Chinese ownership

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.900
have been building since 2020.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.030
- TikTok's been in this
limbo for two years,

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.440
and who knows how many more months

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.420
or years it could stay in this limbo.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.010
- [Narrator] And a panel of US officials

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.410
is torn on how to address them.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.030
If they can't come to an agreement,

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.920
there's another possible solution,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.070
forcing TikTok to become a US company.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.020
Here's what it would
take to make that happen,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.693
and why that move poses
some big challenges.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.890
First, a brief review of how
TikTok's data is managed,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.620
which is the main focus for US officials.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.660
- TikTok's this huge
company, but it's owned

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.150
by a Chinese parent
company called ByteDance.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.290
They run several apps,

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.050
but TikTok is probably their
best known one in the world.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.330
- [Narrator] ByteDance itself
is headquartered in Beijing,

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.330
and is owned by investors
from around the globe.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.130
A Chinese state controlled entity

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:54.060
owns 1% of a Beijing based
subsidiary of ByteDance.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.520
Those connections are what
some are worried about,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.350
and for a couple of reasons.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.730
- The first concern is that

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.710
the Chinese government could order TikTok

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.160
to hand over data about
individual American users.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.980
So what kind of videos they watch,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.900
and maybe even their IP addresses,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.120
which could identify their location.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.170
The second big thing

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.780
is the video recommendation algorithm,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.700
and the idea is that
the Chinese government

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.890
could order TikTok to control

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.590
what videos Americans could watch.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.270
- [Narrator] TikTok says
it has already started

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.400
to address some of those concerns.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.990
The company recently said that

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.210
all US user traffic is now being routed

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.610
through cloud servers operated

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.110
by the US based company Oracle.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.940
And TikTok says that only members

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.450
of its US data security team
have access to that data.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.950
But backups are still being saved

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.810
to other non-Oracle servers in the US

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.490
and Singapore, the company says,

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.050
but it's phasing those out.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.180
As for TikTok's recommendation algorithm,

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.197
that was created by its Chinese
parent company ByteDance.

00:01:51.197 --> 00:01:53.820
TikTok says changes to the
algorithm are monitored

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.970
by Oracle before they're
implemented in the US app.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.380
- So anytime there's a change

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.760
to the algorithm that influences

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.320
what kind of videos Americans see,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.650
they see that Oracle will
have full access to see,

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.570
you know, what the algorithm does.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:07.403
- [Narrator] A spokesperson

00:02:07.403 --> 00:02:08.940
for the Chinese Foreign Ministry

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.710
said in a press conference in November

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.037
in regards to TikTok that

00:02:12.037 --> 00:02:13.380
"Spreading disinformation

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.570
and then using it to
hobble Chinese companies

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.630
has become a go-to tool
for the US government."

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.970
But some US lawmakers still want TikTok

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.520
to have more separation from China.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.640
One option is a divestiture
order or a forced sale,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.010
which could cut ties to Chinese ownership.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:29.910
- The Chinese government would

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:33.090
theoretically have less power over TikTok,

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.400
to force TikTok to do something like spy

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.340
or control what videos Americans watch.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.110
- [Narrator] A divestiture
order is what happened

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.420
to the dating app Grindr in 2019,

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.040
after US officials determined

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.450
that the app's personal data

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.730
could potentially be
exploited for blackmail,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.640
since the majority stakeholder
was a Chinese company.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.790
Here's how the process
has worked in past cases.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.160
First, an executive body branch called

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.100
the Committee on Foreign
Investment in the United States,

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.850
or CFIUS, opens a case with
the involved companies.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.430
This is the panel that's
been talking to TikTok.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.990
It's made up of representatives

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.480
of nine US departments and agencies,

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.920
led by the Treasury,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.020
and reviews foreign transactions to see

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.780
if they might be a national security risk.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.180
After CFIUS reviews a company or merger,

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.880
it can make recommendations
to mitigate those risks,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.950
which can include asking foreign investors

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.560
or owners to sell their
stake in the company.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.050
In extreme cases, it can
also escalate the case

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.170
to the president, who
can order a forced sale.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.810
That owner then has to
find a suitable buyer,

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.880
usually one within the US.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.100
Then the buyer and seller
might have to go back

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.890
to CFIUS in order to
get the sale approved.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.680
Grindr took just over a year
after the order was made

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.810
to find a buyer and get approval.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.240
The president never issued an order.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.160
But TikTok is a much bigger name

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.770
and forcing a sale could
be more complicated.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.170
- There's been nothing of
this scale, this popularity.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.670
Usually, you know, CFIUS deals

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.320
with a lot smaller cases here.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.690
So this is like the case

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.900
of the century for CFIUS
lawyers in Washington in DC.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.920
- [Narrator] A treasury official

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.990
said that CFIUS does not publicly comment

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.200
on transactions that it may
or may not be reviewing.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.310
Officials are worried about

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.100
a number of challenges
facing a forced sale.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.860
One is that the Trump
administration already tried it.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.110
- They have till September
15th to make a deal.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.720
After that, we closed
it up in this country.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.730
- [Narrator] In 2020, that administration

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.580
issued an order that would've
effectively banned TikTok,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.130
unless it sold itself to a US buyer.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.770
But TikTok pushed back and took the order

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.180
to a federal appeals court,

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.330
arguing that the deal denied
the company due process.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.890
It was still tied up in legal issues

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.960
by the time Joe Biden got into office,

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.010
and the order was shelved

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.580
as his administration conducted
its own security review.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.920
But his administration
could face similar pushback

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.050
from TikTok if it tries to force a sale,

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:52.350
and doing so could risk
diluting CFIUS' authority.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.300
- Their power is based on having

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.830
these vague broad powers,

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.170
and if they go to court,
even if they win in court,

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.420
a court might put parameters

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.310
on that power, might define that power,

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.050
'cause the more vague your power is,

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.400
the more powerful it is.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.840
- [Narrator] Even without legal hurdles,

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.640
a sale would also need cooperation

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.990
from the Chinese government,

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.370
which has the power to restrict

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.020
the exports of technology,

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.870
such as TikTok's video
recommendation algorithm.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.110
- If China does not allow
the algorithm to be sold,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.660
then can TikTok continue
operating in the US?

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.770
We don't know.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.720
We're in totally uncharted
waters right now.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.340
- [Narrator] While CFIUS
decides what to do,

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.820
some lawmakers have taken
concerns into their own hands.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:30.870
TikTok has been banned

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.990
on government devices
in a majority of states.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:34.830
And in December,

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.470
the federal government
implemented a similar ban.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.150
- The only sensible next step

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.450
is for this congress
to act to make that ban

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:46.170
across the board for all federal devices.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.280
- [Narrator] At least one bill

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.960
has been introduced to ban TikTok

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.270
entirely in the United States.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:52.620
- That has legal problems too.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.700
That could potentially face
a First Amendment problem.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.080
Can you actually stop,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.140
can you actually ban TikTok
from operating in the US?

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.220
Especially when it has more

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.530
than 100 million American users.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.270
- [Narrator] While TikTok
has made concessions,

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.130
including how its data is managed,

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.050
to get to an agreement with CFIUS,

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.993
talks are ongoing
without a clear deadline.

00:06:13.924 --> 00:06:16.507
(upbeat music)

